    <string name="about_original_title">The original project</string>
    <string name="about_original_text">DBZ Budokai 3 HD Collection is the PC port of the Xbox 360 game by NovaPowers, made with the ReXGlue SDK: the PowerPC code is statically recompiled into a native executable, it is not emulated. Tag Team, online, the mod system and HD texture packs come from there.</string>
    <string name="about_port_title">This port</string>
    <string name="about_port_text">Dragon Fury brings that recompilation to Android: its own launcher (import from the .iso, mods, textures, drivers), touch controls and a GPU path built for phone GPUs (Adreno and Mali), with optional Turnip drivers.</string>
    <string name="about_credits_title">Credits and license</string>
    <string name="about_license">Original project © 2026 NovaPowers, MIT license. Android port by dfdx047.</string>
    <string name="ingame_selftest">Render self-test (diagnostic)</string>
    <string name="ingame_selftest_only_fight">Only during a fight: freezes the picture, toggles each optimization and compares (~3 min). The logs go to Download/ at the end.</string>
    <string name="perf_fps_title">Frame rate</string>
    <string name="perf_fps_sub">30 draws one of every two frames (the game keeps its normal speed). 120 adds a generated frame between every two game frames on 120 Hz screens.</string>
    <string name="perf_fps_120_interp">120 (interp.)</string>
    <string name="perf_fps_120_interp_note">120 FPS interpolated: the game runs at 60 and the screen switches to 120 Hz; one display frame of extra latency and a little extra GPU work (~1-2 ms on fast phones). Needs a steady 60 FPS.</string>
    <string name="perf_fps_120_unavailable">This screen goes up to %1$d Hz: 120 FPS needs a 110 Hz screen or faster.</string>
    <string name="perf_mali_preset">Mali GPU: Dragon Fury starts at 540p with the game effects (bloom, depth of field, FXAA) off, which holds 60 FPS in fights on a Mali-G57. 720p with the effects on runs at about 30.</string>
    <string name="perf_resolution_below">Below 720p the game draws in a corner of the 720p targets and the picture is stretched to the screen (FSR 1 included). 540p keeps every size of the game exact and is the safe choice for Mali GPUs; 360p is the lightest.</string>
